{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Graph]/fn[outgoing_edges]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Graph requires this callback even for a storage-only consumer. The\n delegation test must use only node_path; discovering edges would be\n an unwanted graph access, which this guard rejects. Traversal fixtures\n separately exercise edge discovery."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs#impl[StoredGraph/Graph]/fn[outgoing_edges]` is on an explicit function with a body. That is a permitted form, and the commentary is in fenced citation commentary.\n\nThe reason given is substantive. `Graph` requires the callback, but the storage-only fixture `StoredGraph` is meant to use only `node_path`. The function body is a `panic!` guard, so any execution would mean an unwanted graph access. Zero execution is therefore deliberate and acceptable.\n\nThe explanation agrees with the source:\n- `StoredGraph`'s `EvidenceStorage` methods delegate using only `node_path`.\n- The test `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` calls only `load_evidence` and `store_evidence`.\n- Edge discovery is exercised by other fixtures: `outgoing_edges` is implemented with real behavior in `tests/validation.rs` (`Memory/Graph`), `tests/contracts.rs` (`Application/Graph`) and `tests/agent.rs` (`Memory/Graph`).\n\nThe function has no other citations, so nothing is redundant. I found no gap.",
